(Bug #88's other side: only `not` is a boolean. `-x` really does have `x`'s
 type, so `is_float_expr` and `infer_expr_type` must keep propagating the
 operand's type through `Negate` - a negated float still prints as a float.
 The three paths that were already right are pinned here too: a bare `not`
 in an `if` condition, `is not empty`, and `is not a <type>`.)

a float called ratio is 2.5.
Print -ratio.

a number called depth is 7.
Print -depth.

a text called greeting is "hi".
if not greeting, print "not fired", otherwise print "silent".
if greeting is not empty, print "greeting has content", otherwise print "greeting is blank".
if greeting is not a number, print "greeting is not a number", otherwise print "greeting is a number".

a boolean called ready is false.
if not ready, print "not ready fired", otherwise print "ready".
